    {
      "id": 145836,
      "name": "jffdougan",
      "username": "jffdougan",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jffdougan/{size}/1882_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-08-06T01:26:01.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"dpt\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dpt/48/1922_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> dpt:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Congratulations! What level of school are we talking, and what subject?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Back in a high school again (which I much prefer to middle school, having done both at various times). I'll be the physical sciences half of the science department - at least one physics class of seniors, one introductory physical science class of freshmen, and multiple chemistry classes which will dominantly be juniors. I can't recall offhand whether I have the second-year chem class (functionally, AP Chem) this year or not.</p>\n<p>My previous K-12 experience has all been a more urban setting. I'd only call the one year in a charter school \"big-city\" (since Raleigh-Durham-Chapel Hill, NC is an area of about 600k people all told). This town is definitely more rural, with some of the challenges that might bring.</p>",
      "post_number": 6,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:23:39.998Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
